  "decision": "Do not replace the public runner or extend this prototype on the current hypothesis: the complete real-application gains fail the prospective advancement gate.",
  "advancementRule": "No product adoption. Advance further runner implementation only if both applications reduce complete owner time at least 20% versus upstream Flashwright in both blocks, no observed CPU increase above 5% or sampled memory increase above 10%, and at least one application reaches 2x Playwright in both blocks. Retain all attempts and nonpassing outcomes.",
  "limitations": [
    "Two launches per arm/application; no confidence or tail claim.",
    "Passing-suite subset; arbitrary runner configuration, fixture dependencies, artifacts, retries, timeout cancellation and failure worker replacement remain unimplemented.",
    "Complete wall includes fixture owner and cleanup. Original wait4 CPU is inclusive only of actual reaping; full descendant CPU coverage is unverified. Sampled RSS is not an enforced bound or true peak.",
    "Bun executes the original callbacks through one generated entry module; exact original file module and fixture identities are retained, but this is not general runner equivalence.",
    "Three failed prototype admissions retained separately; they are not timing samples.",
    "Same-suite afterEach registration order and later-declared hooks are not compatible in this private bridge; neither occurs in these corpora.",
    "Result is not an upper bound for every independent runner architecture. Revisit only with a materially different cost-removal hypothesis.",
    "This sanitized checkpoint is a summary of privately retained raw evidence, not a portable raw benchmark snapshot."
  ],
